  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_scope",
      "text": "REAR WHEEL SPEED - one Y harness. RL and RR ABS drops run to the rear VRC in the back-seat area (rear driver-side frame); one screened 4-core output cable runs forward to the 6-way inline DT04-6P near the ECU (IX_WS_REAR). The ECU side owns only the short spur and the DT06-6S mating half (ST185-B-cabin). No bulkhead.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_vrc",
      "text": "VRC NOT DRAWN. The VR conditioner, its enclosure and its M8 panel connectors belong to the enclosure build, not this harness. Loose ends VRC_REAR_IN_L / IN_R / OUT are device endpoints: each lead lands on the matching M8 cable-plug pin when the box is built.",
      "color": "Orange",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 210
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_shield",
      "text": "SHIELDS. Sensor ends float (no S200). At the VRC both input drains are S200-3 and spliced before the plugs: each drain lands on its own IN pin 3, and the combined drain also lands on the OUT screen pin. The OUT drain (S200-4) lands on that same pin and continues on inline pin 5 to SHIELD_B (ECU-B B17). No shield stops at the sensor, the VRC, or the inline. S200 only on terminated ends.",
      "color": "Orange",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 420
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_iso",
      "text": "TWO ISOLATION RULES. 1. The enclosure must not touch chassis - it is part of the screen, not a ground. Nylon mounting hardware. 2. The PCB must not touch the enclosure - nylon standoffs. The board grounds through the output cable only. If either is bonded, the screen picks up supply-ground noise and it will read as a flaky sensor.",
      "color": "Red",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 630
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_coat",
      "text": "MASK THE THREE CONNECTOR LANDINGS AND THE CASE RING-TERMINAL SPOT BEFORE POWDER COAT. The OUT shielding plate and the input screen ring terminals need bare metal. A coated landing silently breaks the screen.",
      "color": "Red",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 810
      }
    }
  ],
